],0,87],[7050992,20390,230,7.323,5.882,[[1,0.758,41,182],[8,0.174,20,36],[4,0.023,22,4],[12,0.023,1,4],[13,0.023,1,4]],[["",53,-2,1],["",53,-2,1],["",54,-2,1],["",53,-2,1],["",45,-2,1],["",53,-2,1],["",53,-2,1],["",53,-2,1]],0,88],[7098836,20392,352,6.141,4.678,[[5,0.662,7,243],[3,0.161,15,58],[1,0.099,42,30],[14,0.048,14,15],[15,0.011,2,2],[10,0.008,12,2],[16,0.005,4,1],[17,0.005,5,1]],[["",19,-1,1]],0,89],[7103527,20395,213,4.157,3.186,[[5,0.583,8,125],[3,0.287,16,61],[14,0.093,15,19],[10,0.028,13,5],[11,0.009,11,1]],[],0,90],[7126218,20402,11,0.407,0.29,[[4,23]],[["8a60e7b7_53b455a7",2,-4,1,"the observed {@code WebContents} is being destroyed."],["bf6d7f72_00738443",19,-4,1,"The first try will always work. The issue is after the first try, the second try will fail because we've set the native bridge to 0 so it won't be notified. Can you please update the description to…"],["e530530d_73e84c22",2,-4,1,"that the observed"],["fa4bc5a8_5fbe3b26",2,-4,1,"."],["6e8c6bd8_befa3181",2,-3,1,"Could you please explain why this check was added and why is it safe to remove the logic to reset the native pointer? IIUC, the check is no longer needed because the native pointer is never reset now."]],0,91],[7115618,20402,50,2.11,1.633,[[1,0.845,43,44],[18,0.069,0,3],[13,0.052,2,2],[19,0.034,0,1]],[["05930b2d_cd959e68",21,-6,1,"Lets add a comment we can only enter this branch if the user selected the BNPL chip before amount extraction returned because if AE returned and there was no final checkout amount value the chip…"],["54fcac02_0801b44c",55,-6,1,"Will this be different from kBnplFetchVcnProgressDialog? Same question below"],["7e8957e1_a0bbe2e6",56,-6,1,"Lets add a TODO?"],["b0fe80c3_f138cad8",21,-6,0,"This currently just grays out the bnpl chip. We also need to switch to the select issuer view with no valid issuers. We can probably set a ``` bool…"]],0,92],[7127932,20405,58,1.144,0.818,[[5,0.55,9,32],[3,0.45,17,26]],[["87fa802e_3cce3e16",19,-3,0,"What happens when the user clicks the back arrow here?"]],0,93],[7123178,20412,717,13.232,10.82,[[1,0.453,44,330],[8,0.415,21,295],[4,0.069,24,48],[12,0.027,2,18],[13,0.027,3,18],[3,0.009,18,6]],[["12b56399_5c3cc6c8",21,-13,1,"Lets merge these calls and let the UI handle it? we can pass either issuer context or nullopt based on whether we have extracted an amount, and similarly we can use…"],["20eafb6b_5ea0230f",21,-13,1,"Should this just be ``` if (ongoing_flow_state_) { ongoing_flow_state_->final_checkout_amount = std::move(extracted_amount); } ``` Since in the accept before AE returned case, we'd have a flow state…"],["25d61a91_a59afe1d",25,-13,1,"We also need to check if the amount doesn't exist and show an error screen?"],["c1aa9d19_49928490",25,-13,1,"Lets show an error? This shouldn't happen though, but probably a good safety check."],["e83c09c7_7fd65b40",57,-13,1,"Optional isn't needed - base::span can be empty and that's the \"null state\""],["45ebba60_b525ae33",21,-8,1,"If there is no available checkout amount, notify the UI."],["4d1b27d9_178b2afe",21,-8,1,"Since in the timeout reached case we also won't have an extracted amount, lets just use not having an extracted amount for this if-branch?"],["94961941_026f1591",21,-8,1,"If an amount was extracted, notify the UI so it can handle it based on whether the amount is supported or not, and where in the UI flow the user is at the moment."],["aba44cc8_1d54b350",25,-8,0,"Lets move this above line 554?"],["ba0fa7a6_e4b4b35d",21,-8,1,"Lets put this on a newline to make it easier to read"],["60316db5_ede4c9c4",21,-6,1,"FYI, if `extracted_amount` is nullopt, this will crash. I'm fine putting this to a separate CL but lets add a TODO"],["67de214d_92c60565",58,-6,1,"Would it make sense to add a `NOTIMPLEMENTED` here? (Same for WebView)"],["dbea4aac_ca98a0eb",59,-6,1,"UpdateTouchToFillProgressScreenOnAmountReturned maybe?"],["ddc528d8_33509e42",21,-6,1,"``` // `ongoing_flow_state_` being present indicates the user accepted the BNPL // suggestion. ```"],["45e05eef_4d52a3dc",26,-2,1,"Unrelated to this CL, just use `ResourceMapper::MapToJavaDrawableId` in the `CreateJavaBnplIssuerContextFromNative` instead of passing a controller to this method. We can use…"],["4c9364b4_a7ff1cb9",25,-2,1,"This method is called when the transaction amount is extracted. Can we have a generic method `onPurchaseAmountExtracted`?"],["6a180669_06be72b7",25,-2,1,"Consider renaming to `onPurchaseAmountExtracted`. This method doesn't update the screen, it closes the progress screen and shows the BNPL issuers screen."],["f05ee254_60568a86",25,-2,0,"Please extract into a helper method if you don't end up merging 2 methods into 1."],["0e9cbb9f_51546bbb",21,-1,1,"We should pass the list of BNPL issuers here instead of an empty list and cache them on the Java side. The only reason we don't pass the list of BNPL issuers immediately is because the transactions…"]],0,94],[7154302,20412,73,2.344,1.853,[[8,0.934,22,69],[10,0.066,14,4]],[["b1d765bb_9bc5741e",25,-3,1,"`else if (extractedAmount == null) {`?"],["d309f8a9_c74dcf4f",25,-3,1,"Why is this needed? I assume the case where an amount is extracted but isn't supported by any issuer would be an else if branch where we set the chip as gray etc"]],0,95],[7158394,20416,313,7.579,6.176,[[8,23]],[["1bf5b502_c05f2c90",25,-5,1,"Can you please add a comment here that this checks if there is *any* issuer that is enabled, if there is then the chip isn't disabled on the home screen"],["07e443d1_a47871f1",25,-4,0,"You'll hit a merge conflict with this CL: crrev.com/c/7162897, I would recommend waiting till this chain of metrics CL chain gets merged"],["61d301fc_d8db826e",25,-4,1,"Let's just show home screen and early return if the current screen is not BNPL: ``` if (mModel.get(CURRENT_SCREEN) != BNPL_ISSUER_SELECTION_SCREEN)) { showHomeScreen(); return; } ```"],["b0c3728e_f20f6b41",25,-4,1,"Please create a helper method to find the BNPL suggestion. A better approach would be to store BNPL suggestion is a private member."],["174357b9_aa556fc3",25,-3,1,"When BNPL suggestion model is `null` here? Is it possible that `onPurchaseAmountExtracted` is called when IBAN or loyalty card bottom sheet is shown?"],["5fb6716f_6add5ca7",60,-3,1,"After bnpl suggestion model is stored as a private variable, you can use `mCoordinator.getMediatorForTesting().getBnplSuggestionModelForTesting()`."],["ba8d3014_27b35c85",25,-3,1,"You can store bnpl suggestion model as well and remove `findBnplSuggestionModel` because it doesn't change as well."],["90aa6668_9c784b3d",25,0,1,"IIUC `mBnplSuggestionModel` can't be `null` here. Ideally we should just call `assumeNotNull` here."]],0,96],[7181869,20416,282,11.951,9.625,[[1,0.941,45,267],[17,0.059,6,15]],[["0128d872_1ff83979",61,-3,1,"Please don't forget to update go/payments-autofill-uma"]],0,97],[7206250,20418,34,1.326,1.047,[[4,0.658,25,23],[20,0.342,0,11]],[],0,98],[7201145,20418,50,1.144,0.818,[[5,0.472,10,24],[21,0.358,2,18],[3,0.17,19,8]],[],0,98],[7204300,20423,19,1.154,0.872,[[1,0.783,46,15],[20,0.217,0,4]],[["96015691_323885f4",62,-5,1,"Is this change related to this CL? This revert will re-add these lines: crrev.com/c/7206250"],["b2b86e2d_84fb8471",63,-5,1,"Let's keep this todo."]],0,99],[7226295,20426,23,0.721,0.543,[[4,25]],[["d65ed54a_8163a764",64,-1,0,"Why is this needed?"]],0,100],[7234254,20428,15,0.447,0.304,[[1,47]],[],0,101],[7242094,20432,19,0.198,0.14,[[0,9]],[["a261e3ef_00f58421",65,0,1,"This is already enabled by default, we shouldn't ramp it up https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:components/autofill/core/common/autofill_payments_features.cc;l=75"],["ac7a6d20_add9f9bf",65,0,1,"Lets add klarna externally linked too?"]],0,102],[7248999,20433,51,2.11,1.633,[[1,0.678,48,35],[6,0.322,4,16]],[["057da8ca_76eaa710",45,0,1,"indent -2"],["13dcaee4_32533cf6",66,0,1,"indent -2 (auto-formatter doesn't catch this because the lines weren't modified)"]],0,103],[7254550,20438,27,1.154,0.872,[[1,0.793,49,22],[8,0.207,24,5]]